# Prepared911 Personal Workspace

This multi-root workspace contains:

- `prepared911`: application repository and project source of truth
- `axon911-frontend`: related frontend source and package history
- `vault-core-ux`: related design-system source and package history
- `personal-harness`: private orchestration, critics, and review contracts

## Resolve roots

Before reviewing or editing, locate the Prepared911 root by finding all of:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `turbo/AGENTS.md`
- `turbo/apps/docs/AGENTS.md`
- `turbo/packages/ui-core/package.json`

Do not assume the current shell directory is the Prepared911 root.

Locate the personal harness root by finding:

- `docs/review-contract.md`
- `.cursor/skills/adversarial-review/SKILL.md`

## Source priority

Prepared911 repository instructions, public APIs, tests, generated API data,
and actual behavior take precedence over personal harness guidance. The
personal harness coordinates repository skills; it does not redefine project
coding standards.

When a task explicitly targets `axon911-frontend` or `vault-core-ux`, read and
follow that repository's own `AGENTS.md` and local instructions. Never assume
Prepared911-specific implementation rules apply unchanged to another root.

All four workspace roots are eligible read/write implementation targets:

- `prepared911`
- `axon911-frontend`
- `vault-core-ux`
- `personal-harness` (only when the user explicitly asks to update the harness
  or the task names harness runtime verification)

Before editing, identify the target root or roots from the user's request and
read each target repository's instructions. If the target is genuinely
ambiguous and choosing incorrectly would change repository state, ask which
root to modify.

Do not copy code between repositories without checking ownership, API
compatibility, licensing, and repository-specific rules.

## Plan and implementation contracts

- Implementation plans follow `docs/plan-contract.md`. Prefer `/plan-check`
  before implementing. Use `/adversarial-review mode=plan` for `T2` plans.
- Implementation tasks follow `docs/implementation-contract.md`: resolve the
  root, run affected verification, fix every instance at the shared layer,
  attach rendered evidence for user-visible changes, and dispatch a
  fresh-context review at the blast-radius tier the change requires.
- Harness runtime work also follows `docs/runtime-contract.md`. Local hooks
  provide cooperative assurance, not atomic Git enforcement.
- Blast-radius tiers (`T0` / `T1` / `T2`) are defined in
  `docs/routing-matrix.md` and judged by callers, not file counts.

## Formal review

For a formal plan or implementation review, invoke `adversarial-review`.
Review critics and the adjudicator are read-only. Fixes require a separate task.
Do not run the full critic panel for ordinary implementation work unless the
user asks for a formal review or explicitly invokes `/adversarial-review`.
Ordinary changes still need a fresh-context pass at their tier; authoring-
context self-review is not enough.

The design-system and frontend-architecture critics must benchmark against:

- `turbo/apps/docs/mdx/design`
- `turbo/apps/docs/mdx/engineering`
- `turbo/apps/docs/generated/component-api-registry.json`
- Relevant docs app source and rendered examples

Do not apply Next.js-only guidance from the docs app to Vite applications.

## Safety

- Do not modify `personal-harness` during an implementation task unless the
  user explicitly asks to update the harness.
- Do not modify `prepared911` during a review-only task.
- Preserve all pre-existing changes in every repository, especially dirty
  working trees.
- Before implementation in any repository, follow that repository's branch and
  worktree policy.
- Report the workspace root containing every modified file.
